// Two modules may use the same member names. Both of these failed:
//
//  - a #local in each: the names ride in the #define buffer, which #end was
//    supposed to roll back and did not -- "local Now is already defined"
//  - a #param in each: the second was taken at start-up for a saved value of
//    the FIRST (a param override is found by name) and written through a
//    global index -- onto the program's State, and every loose rule after it
//    stopped
#module A
  #param Flags = 3
  #local Now = Flags + 1
  #variable Seen
  Seen = Now
#end
#module B
  #param Flags = 0x20
  #local Now = Flags + 2
  #variable Seen
  Seen = Now
#end
#A a
#B b
#variable G = 0
G = 7
